    "body": "What would be the best approach to ensure that allauth Email Addresses Model is GDPR compliant?\r\nIssues:\r\nEncryption - This seems problematic since it seems hard to change the current model to support it outside of allauth core package\r\nDeletion - seems fine to me since this is tied to the user so how you handle user deletion you can change the email field value.\r\nAnonymization - This seems fine to me since you can set unique value that has nothing to do with user.\r\n\r\nWhat worries me is the part where email is stored in a separate model where you cannot encrypt the field.",
